WEBVTT

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:29.246
I'm Sylvia Ront, and this
is FNN's continuing coverage

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:31.465
of the destruction
of Pakled Planet.

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:34.947
What we know at this hour:
Starfleet Captain Carol Freeman

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.081
&lt;i&gt;stands accused of orchestrating a devastating attack&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:39.473
&lt;i&gt;on the Pakled capital,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:42.781
a place they call
"Big Strong City."

00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:45.479
The USS &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
remains in spacedock,

00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:47.916
impounded for further
investigation;

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.962
her crew, on temporary leave

00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:52.182
while their captain
stands trial.

00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:53.748
- Why would Freeman do this?
- No comment.

00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:55.359
- What did you hear?
- I said no comment.

00:00:55.402 --> 00:00:56.708
- Please, a little respect.
- Did she hate Pakleds?

00:00:56.751 --> 00:00:58.188
out of our way!

00:00:58.231 --> 00:01:00.581
And the latest
shocking development,

00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:02.279
new surveillance footage retrieved

00:01:02.322 --> 00:01:04.890
&lt;i&gt;from the attack that appears&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to place Freeman&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:07.501
&lt;i&gt;on the ground at the time&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;of the bombing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:07.545 --> 00:01:10.852
&lt;i&gt;In "lighter" news, a swarm&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;of incandescent verugament&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:10.896 --> 00:01:12.550
&lt;i&gt;will be illuminating&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Earth tomorrow...&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:12.593 --> 00:01:14.291
Beckett!

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:17.163
Screens can just be
turned off, you know.

00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:18.686
I can't take this anymore.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.558
Everyone's acting like
the trial's already over,

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.082
when there is no way that Mom
did anything wrong.

00:01:23.126 --> 00:01:25.040
Look, you and I both know that,

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.478
and plenty of people
in the courtroom know it, too.

00:01:27.521 --> 00:01:30.045
You just need to be patient
and trust in the system.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.439
Oh, you mean the same system
that's now putting her on trial?

00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:33.875
Oh, yeah, yeah,

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:35.790
I frickin' love the system.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.618
Ah, ah, ah. Hey, hey, hey, hey,
why don't you go out for bit?

00:01:37.662 --> 00:01:40.317
We don't get home that often.
You can maybe go for a walk,

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.927
breathe some non-recycled air.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.103
Home for you.
I didn't grow up here.

00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:46.801
I just meant Earth. It's rare
that you get back here.

00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:49.587
Ugh, the longer I'm off a ship,
the more useless I feel.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.197
Like that. Like that big,
dumb red thing.

00:01:51.241 --> 00:01:53.330
Beckett, you know that's
the Golden Gate Bridge.

00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:55.070
Nobody drives anymore.
Why do you need a bridge?

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.550
This planet's wack.

00:01:56.594 --> 00:01:58.900
People like the bridge.
I like the bridge.

00:02:01.512 --> 00:02:03.514
Ah, Admiral Buenamigo.

00:02:03.557 --> 00:02:06.778
&lt;i&gt;Alonzo. I am afraid&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I'm the bearer of bad news.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:06.821 --> 00:02:08.910
What? What-What's the news?
Oh, hey, Uncle Les.

00:02:08.954 --> 00:02:11.304
Beckett. I just received word,

00:02:11.348 --> 00:02:14.220
the judge assigned
to Carol's case is, uh...

00:02:14.264 --> 00:02:16.266
Mith bin Tong.

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:18.006
What? She's that
"planet's rights" lunatic.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.704
Dad, we got to get Mom
out of this trial.

00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:21.053
We got to have faith
in Starfleet.

00:02:21.096 --> 00:02:23.011
The truth will come out.

00:02:23.055 --> 00:02:25.797
If you won't do something,
then I will.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.146
Wait, wait,
wait, no, ah.

00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:30.367
&lt;i&gt;-I don't know why&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.456
&lt;i&gt;you keep breakable objects&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;in the house anymore.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:34.545
- Neither do I.
-

00:03:51.926 --> 00:03:54.842
-

00:03:56.714 --> 00:03:58.759
Oh, God, vineyard flies.

00:03:58.803 --> 00:04:00.457
Ugh. I hate being home.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.285
Dude, are you even listening
to what I'm telling you?

00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:03.808
The captain's
getting railroaded, man.

00:04:03.851 --> 00:04:05.723
I have to do something
before it's too late.

00:04:05.766 --> 00:04:07.681
- Well, count me in.
- Really?

00:04:07.725 --> 00:04:09.335
Usually, it takes
way more convincing.

00:04:09.379 --> 00:04:10.989
I'll do anything to get away
from these raisins.

00:04:11.032 --> 00:04:12.251
It's already
gonna take me a month

00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:13.426
to get the smell out of my hair.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.906
Hey, Bradward.

00:04:14.949 --> 00:04:17.387
Want to test the sweetness
of my bushel?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.085
Ugh, fine, Genevieve.

00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:22.914
Just give it 43 more sun hours
at 21 degrees brix.

00:04:22.957 --> 00:04:25.177
Oh, okay.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.353
Uh, when you said your family
had vineyards,

00:04:27.397 --> 00:04:28.789
I just assumed it was for wine.

00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:31.488
Oh, I wish.
No, we Boimlers dry grapes.

00:04:31.531 --> 00:04:34.186
Just dry them
and dry them and dry them

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:36.406
till they're all shriveled
and hopeless

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:38.059
and stuck on Earth forever.

00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:41.585
Bradward, all these varietals
are so confusing.

00:04:41.628 --> 00:04:43.630
Take me to the privacy
of the pickery shed

00:04:43.674 --> 00:04:45.284
and explain them to me.

00:04:45.328 --> 00:04:47.242
Come on, Mandolina,
red goes in the red bucket,

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.896
white in the white,
you know that.

00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:51.986
How do they not see
this is a setup?

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.988
We were nowhere near
Pakled Planet when it blew.

00:04:54.032 --> 00:04:56.556
I mean, she was saving
another ship, for Kirk's sake.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.210
Okay, we know it doesn't track,

00:04:58.253 --> 00:04:59.472
but the ship's logs
got corrupted

00:04:59.516 --> 00:05:01.169
by the Laapeerian debris field.

00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:02.823
It makes it look like
she's covering something up.

00:05:02.867 --> 00:05:05.130
Wait, so they just need
our logs? I have logs.

00:05:05.173 --> 00:05:07.132
No. We need the official
senior staff logs,

00:05:07.175 --> 00:05:08.568
not, like,
what you had for lunch.

00:05:08.612 --> 00:05:10.135
No, no, no. My logs
are crazy detailed.

00:05:10.178 --> 00:05:11.658
Every night,
I'd listen to the captain's

00:05:11.702 --> 00:05:12.877
and re-record them
for my own reference.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:13.965
What?

00:05:14.008 --> 00:05:15.140
Yeah. The official stardates,

00:05:15.183 --> 00:05:16.489
systems, personnel,

00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:18.012
it's all in there,
stowed by my bunk.

00:05:18.056 --> 00:05:19.884
Oh, my God, Boimler, wait,
that is so nerdy

00:05:19.927 --> 00:05:21.538
- and so clutch right now.
-

00:05:21.581 --> 00:05:23.235
So, all we have to do
is get your PADDs,

00:05:23.278 --> 00:05:25.193
and we clear her name
with some surprise evidence.

00:05:25.237 --> 00:05:27.021
Take that,
conservative military court.

00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:28.588
But we're grounded.

00:05:28.632 --> 00:05:30.460
Plus, we don't even know
where the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is.

00:05:30.503 --> 00:05:32.244
It's in dry dock?

00:05:32.287 --> 00:05:34.464
Yeah, but which dry dock?
There's, like, a bajillion.

00:05:34.507 --> 00:05:36.944
And, besides, they probably only
kept on a small skeleton crew

00:05:36.988 --> 00:05:38.685
of engineers to help dock it,
and that's it.

00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:40.165
Engineers?

00:05:40.208 --> 00:05:41.427
Rutherford!

00:05:41.471 --> 00:05:43.777
Bradward, I'm soaked in juice,

00:05:43.821 --> 00:05:45.910
and I need help getting naked.

00:05:45.953 --> 00:05:47.781
Just spray off
with the hose, Lianne.

00:05:51.524 --> 00:05:53.352
&lt;i&gt;&lt;i&gt;Say "gumbo."&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:53.396 --> 00:05:54.788
Gumbo!

00:05:56.311 --> 00:05:58.096
So, after lunch,
where should we go next?

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:00.533
I mean, should we go back to
the Grand Canyon? Is that crazy?

00:06:00.577 --> 00:06:03.493
We could take in
a London Kings game, or... Ooh!

00:06:03.536 --> 00:06:05.320
Want to go see
historical Bozeman?

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.671
The site of Zefram
Cochrane's first warp flight?

00:06:07.714 --> 00:06:09.455
Um, yes, please.

00:06:09.499 --> 00:06:11.501
Man, I can't believe you never
visited any Earth stuff

00:06:11.544 --> 00:06:12.937
when you were at the Academy.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.591
Oh, I was so focused
on my studies,

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.984
I never left San Francisco.
I just...

00:06:18.508 --> 00:06:21.032
Man, I can't believe this.

00:06:21.075 --> 00:06:23.077
Those prosecutors
are gonna look so stupid

00:06:23.121 --> 00:06:24.862
when the captain
gets proved innocent.

00:06:24.905 --> 00:06:26.820
I wonder how Mariner's
taking it.

00:06:26.864 --> 00:06:28.082
Oh, I'm taking it...

00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:29.997
taking it to the limit.

00:06:31.521 --> 00:06:33.653
Did you, did you time
your entrance to say that?

00:06:33.697 --> 00:06:35.481
- What? No.
- Oh, yeah, she did.

00:06:35.525 --> 00:06:37.222
No. I mean, like,
only, like, a few seconds.

00:06:37.265 --> 00:06:38.658
It was at least a minute.
I was like,

00:06:38.702 --> 00:06:39.964
"Why are we hiding by the door?"

00:06:40.007 --> 00:06:41.748
Would you just go get us
some chairs?

00:06:43.663 --> 00:06:46.361
Hmm, I don't know,
sneaking into the impound dock

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:49.321
- doesn't sound very Starfleet.
-

00:06:49.364 --> 00:06:50.540
Well, neither does throwing
the captain into prison

00:06:50.583 --> 00:06:52.063
for a crime she didn't commit.

00:06:52.106 --> 00:06:53.499
-
- Okay, well, let's just

00:06:53.543 --> 00:06:54.631
go tell the court
about Boimler's logs.

00:06:54.674 --> 00:06:56.067
Why, so they can bury them? No.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.938
Something went down
on Pakled Planet,

00:06:57.982 --> 00:06:59.810
and they want a &lt;i&gt;Cali&lt;/i&gt;-class
captain to take the fall.

00:06:59.853 --> 00:07:01.594
The bridge crew
are under constant attack.

00:07:01.638 --> 00:07:03.161
-
- It's up to us to do something.

00:07:03.204 --> 00:07:04.597
I know where the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is.

00:07:04.641 --> 00:07:05.772
I got a glance
at the orbital coordinates

00:07:05.816 --> 00:07:06.773
when we were docking.

00:07:06.817 --> 00:07:08.166
It's only 19 digits.

00:07:08.209 --> 00:07:09.907
Yes, Ruthy Ruth! There we go.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.039
But the only way up
to that dry dock

00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:14.912
is via an encrypted transporter
at a secure compound.

00:07:14.955 --> 00:07:16.783
How are we gonna get in?

00:07:16.827 --> 00:07:18.611
Geez, don't cry, man.
We'll figure something out.

00:07:18.655 --> 00:07:20.874
-
- Nice little kick.

00:07:26.576 --> 00:07:29.666
Uh, so we're gonna have to get
past the transporter chief.

00:07:29.709 --> 00:07:31.668
I heard he's long-time
Starfleet security.

00:07:31.711 --> 00:07:33.626
- He could be intense.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold up.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.628
We have to face
some kind of psycho badass?

00:07:35.672 --> 00:07:37.978
Look, we've got the numbers
and the element of surprise.

00:07:38.022 --> 00:07:39.545
This is for the captain.

00:07:41.808 --> 00:07:44.245
Well, ahoy, there.
Come in, come in.

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.204
Don't let the door hit you
where the Big Bang

00:07:46.247 --> 00:07:47.901
split you.

00:07:47.945 --> 00:07:50.208
Yup.
Let me just get over here.

00:07:50.251 --> 00:07:52.384
Chief Carlton Dennis
at your service.

00:07:52.427 --> 00:07:54.125
You can call me Denny.

00:07:54.168 --> 00:07:56.780
So, what brings y'all to
my dusty old transporter pad?

00:07:56.823 --> 00:07:58.303
You kids from the Academy?

00:07:58.346 --> 00:07:59.957
Uh, yeah, that's right,
we were just, uh,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.569
hoping to learn...
about your transporter.

00:08:03.613 --> 00:08:05.353
Say no more.
If there's one thing I've got

00:08:05.397 --> 00:08:06.964
in this joint, it's gout.

00:08:07.007 --> 00:08:08.835
But also transporters.

00:08:08.879 --> 00:08:11.272
Come on, let's give you
the tour. Here we go.

00:08:11.316 --> 00:08:12.709
We can't tie this guy up.

00:08:12.752 --> 00:08:14.580
He's, like, the sweetest
old man in the world.

00:08:14.624 --> 00:08:17.061
I know, I know,
but we have no choice, okay?

00:08:17.104 --> 00:08:18.845
- Just distract him for me.
- Whoa!

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:20.586
These transporters are classics.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:22.632
- Did you restore these?
- Yeah.

00:08:22.675 --> 00:08:24.329
I'm a bit of a buffer buff.

00:08:24.372 --> 00:08:27.419
Working on these beauties
is what kept me going when my...

00:08:27.462 --> 00:08:29.421
when my wife Jane passed.

00:08:29.464 --> 00:08:30.814
Guys, I can't.
You got to do it.

00:08:30.857 --> 00:08:32.293
No way. He's like my grandpa.

00:08:32.337 --> 00:08:34.600
- He's everyone's grandpa.
Butterscotch?

00:08:36.428 --> 00:08:37.995
Sure, yeah, thanks, Denny.

00:08:38.038 --> 00:08:40.301
It's so rare that
I get visitors here.

00:08:40.345 --> 00:08:42.565
You kids are the real treat.

00:08:42.608 --> 00:08:45.611
Yeah, usually people only come
in looking to knock me out and

00:08:45.655 --> 00:08:48.005
use my transporter to beam
to a restricted ship.

00:08:48.048 --> 00:08:49.659
You wouldn't know anything
about that...

00:08:49.702 --> 00:08:51.922
-
- ...would you?

00:08:51.965 --> 00:08:54.533
-

00:08:54.577 --> 00:08:57.754
Aw, there, there,
don't-don't cry. Okay.

00:08:57.797 --> 00:08:59.451
I wasn't gonna stun you.

00:08:59.494 --> 00:09:02.454
It's all right. You know what?
I'll make some soup.

00:09:04.238 --> 00:09:06.371
&lt;i&gt;Look, I don't blame you&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;one bit for trying to help&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:06.414 --> 00:09:08.242
your captain.
I've been following her trial.

00:09:08.286 --> 00:09:09.896
I don't buy those charges
for a second.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.855
So, can you transport us
up to our ship?

00:09:11.898 --> 00:09:15.641
I would, but I can't
'cause of the damned verugament.

00:09:15.685 --> 00:09:17.338
- Veruga-what?
- It's been all over the news.

00:09:17.382 --> 00:09:20.124
A big swarm of glowing
space critters

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:21.821
migrating right past Earth.

00:09:21.865 --> 00:09:24.781
They create a natural
scattering field that interferes

00:09:24.824 --> 00:09:26.434
with the transporter.

00:09:26.478 --> 00:09:28.785
I'm afraid all surface-to-space
beaming is down.

00:09:28.828 --> 00:09:31.483
What? We can't let
some space bugs stop us.

00:09:31.526 --> 00:09:33.790
Sorry, kiddo. The only way
you're getting to that dry dock

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:35.008
is in a ship.

00:09:35.052 --> 00:09:36.880
So, we didn't save the captain

00:09:36.923 --> 00:09:40.274
and missed a once-in-a-lifetime
trip to historical Bozeman?

00:09:40.318 --> 00:09:42.494
Oh, you would've loved Bozeman.

00:09:42.537 --> 00:09:44.714
Oh, the reenactors.

00:09:44.757 --> 00:09:46.716
Oh, they got this replica &lt;i&gt;Phoenix&lt;/i&gt; ride.

00:09:46.759 --> 00:09:48.848
You know, folks can just
take it up into orbit. Ah...

00:09:48.892 --> 00:09:51.503
Wait, you can't
transport us to space,

00:09:51.546 --> 00:09:54.462
but what about Montana?

00:10:03.863 --> 00:10:05.517
&lt;i&gt;ZEFRAM COCHRANE &lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Hello, explorers,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.607
&lt;i&gt;and welcome to the 21st century.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:08.651 --> 00:10:10.130
&lt;i&gt;We hope you enjoy yourself&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:10.174 --> 00:10:13.220
&lt;i&gt;and make a first contact&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;with fun.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:13.264 --> 00:10:15.483
Ooh, ooh, they're just like
the 21st century.

00:10:15.527 --> 00:10:16.702
It's just like
post-World War III.

00:10:16.746 --> 00:10:18.443
Oh, my gosh,

00:10:18.486 --> 00:10:19.879
there's the Crash-n-Burn Bar

00:10:19.923 --> 00:10:21.446
with its famous
one-song jukebox.

00:10:21.489 --> 00:10:22.534
Look, there's the ship

00:10:22.577 --> 00:10:24.101
that the Vulcans came down in.

00:10:24.144 --> 00:10:25.102
Whoa.

00:10:25.145 --> 00:10:26.277
C-Can I try that?

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.974
I-It would be illogical not to.

00:10:28.018 --> 00:10:30.324
Sorry, guys, we came for that.

00:10:37.767 --> 00:10:41.205
- Ah. Wow.
- Whoo.

00:10:49.822 --> 00:10:53.043
&lt;i&gt;Oh, hi. I'm just&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;finishing up some repairs,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:53.086 --> 00:10:55.698
&lt;i&gt;and you should&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;finish up any snacks,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:55.741 --> 00:10:58.526
&lt;i&gt;as no food or beverages are allowed inside the&lt;/i&gt; Phoenix.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:01.181
Hey, guys, are we sure
we can even fly this thing?

00:11:01.225 --> 00:11:03.618
I mean, you only have to be
100 centimeters to ride.

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:05.577
Look, a ship's a ship. Once
we're out of the atmosphere,

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.579
Rutherford can override
the automation. Right, Ruthy?

00:11:07.622 --> 00:11:09.799
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, yup, you got it.

00:11:11.801 --> 00:11:13.106
All right.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.542
- Here we g...
Okay, oh, boy.

00:11:14.586 --> 00:11:15.630
Here we go, Gavin.

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:17.284
You're really doing this, huh?

00:11:17.328 --> 00:11:18.416
-
- Oh, crap.

00:11:18.459 --> 00:11:19.852
Hey, buddy, um,

00:11:19.896 --> 00:11:21.549
you should really get on
a different &lt;i&gt;Phoenix.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:21.593 --> 00:11:23.421
Oh, no, no, no, no,
the guy clearly told me,

00:11:23.464 --> 00:11:24.944
"Single rider,
ship number five."

00:11:24.988 --> 00:11:26.467
I don't want to get in trouble.

00:11:26.511 --> 00:11:28.034
Hey, we don't go past
warp one, right?

00:11:29.383 --> 00:11:30.950
I'm sorry,
I'm just a little nervous

00:11:30.994 --> 00:11:32.169
'cause, you know, I'm not good
with spaceflight.

00:11:34.867 --> 00:11:36.695
All right, buckos,

00:11:36.739 --> 00:11:39.306
prepare for your trek
amongst the stars.

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:41.613
Oh, before I forget...

00:11:41.656 --> 00:11:43.223
Let's rock and roll.

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:46.966
&lt;i&gt;♪ I like to dream, yes...&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:11:49.795 --> 00:11:52.102
&lt;i&gt;♪ Right between&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the sound machine...&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:11:54.017 --> 00:11:55.975
&lt;i&gt;♪ On a cloud of sound&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I drift in the night&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:11:56.019 --> 00:11:57.281
&lt;i&gt;♪ To the stars away from here&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:11:57.324 --> 00:11:58.586
&lt;i&gt;♪ Well, you don't know...&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.936
I think we're
supposed to stay seated.

00:11:59.979 --> 00:12:01.981
First stage separation complete.

00:12:02.025 --> 00:12:05.811
Let's bring what I like to call
"the warp core" online.

00:12:05.855 --> 00:12:07.334
Sorry, Mr. Cochrane.

00:12:07.378 --> 00:12:08.814
&lt;i&gt;♪ You don't know what...&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:12:08.858 --> 00:12:10.381
Wh-What are you doing?

00:12:10.424 --> 00:12:11.686
W-W-Wow,

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:12.818
would you look at that

00:12:12.862 --> 00:12:14.646
&lt;i&gt;beautiful blue marble?&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:14.689 --> 00:12:16.430
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:12:16.474 --> 00:12:18.345
&lt;i&gt;It's working.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;It's kind of working.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:18.389 --> 00:12:20.565
&lt;i&gt;All right. Inputting dry dock coordinates.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:20.608 --> 00:12:22.523
Prepare to make history.

00:12:22.567 --> 00:12:23.873
Here we go.

00:12:25.875 --> 00:12:27.659
Wh-Wh-What are you doing?

00:12:27.702 --> 00:12:29.400
&lt;i&gt;♪ Last night I held&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Aladdin's lamp...&lt;/i&gt;♪

00:12:40.715 --> 00:12:42.979
&lt;i&gt;Oh, wow.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Whoa.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:47.853 --> 00:12:50.987
&lt;i&gt;Thanks&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;for riding with me, explorers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.597
Please exit on the right,

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.512
and take all your
belongings with you.

00:12:54.555 --> 00:12:56.035
- Sorry about that, Gav.
-

00:12:56.079 --> 00:12:57.689
Top secret Starfleet business
going on here.

00:12:57.732 --> 00:12:59.212
Don't worry, man.
I'll reengage the automation

00:12:59.256 --> 00:13:00.300
and get you back down to Earth.

00:13:00.344 --> 00:13:01.693
Wait, don't.

00:13:01.736 --> 00:13:03.564
This is my ship now.

00:13:03.608 --> 00:13:05.653
I'm not Gavin
the botanist anymore.

00:13:05.697 --> 00:13:08.047
No, I am Gavin the pilot,

00:13:08.091 --> 00:13:11.311
and I am going
to explore the galaxy!

00:13:11.355 --> 00:13:12.573
- Hell yeah.
- Respect, man.

00:13:12.617 --> 00:13:13.966
Woo-hoo!

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.012
This won't be the last
you hear of me.

00:13:22.409 --> 00:13:24.194
Okay, all right,
it should be right...

00:13:24.237 --> 00:13:26.109
Yes! My copies of all
the captain's logs

00:13:26.152 --> 00:13:28.589
going back to stardate 58018.7.

00:13:28.633 --> 00:13:30.026
This should be more than enough.

00:13:30.069 --> 00:13:31.636
Oh, Boims, I will never
make fun of you

00:13:31.679 --> 00:13:33.333
for this kind of stuff again.

00:13:33.377 --> 00:13:35.031
Okay, let me see the one
from the day of the bombing.

00:13:35.074 --> 00:13:36.771
&lt;i&gt;BOIMLER &lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is en route&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:36.815 --> 00:13:37.990
&lt;i&gt;to the Laapeerian system&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to assist the&lt;/i&gt; Archimedes

00:13:38.034 --> 00:13:39.426
&lt;i&gt;in a first contact.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.298
Yes! That is exactly
what we need to save Mom.

00:13:41.341 --> 00:13:43.561
&lt;i&gt;Oh, and I think I heard Ransom&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;say my name today.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:43.604 --> 00:13:45.563
&lt;i&gt;He might've said,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;"Boiler," but still,&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:45.606 --> 00:13:47.652
&lt;i&gt;name recognition! Oh, my God!&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:47.695 --> 00:13:48.871
What? What was, what was that?

00:13:48.914 --> 00:13:50.307
Oh, yeah, no, I always add

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.048
little personal details to them.
Makes them fun.

00:13:52.091 --> 00:13:54.354
&lt;i&gt;Got caught sniffing&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the captain's chair again.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:54.398 --> 00:13:55.747
They're... they're all
like this?

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.270
No, no, no,
that's just one or two.

00:13:57.314 --> 00:13:59.359
The rest of them
are very professional.

00:13:59.403 --> 00:14:01.971
The alien atmosphere &lt;i&gt;is giving me insane gas.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:02.014 --> 00:14:03.929
&lt;i&gt;Got to be better about hiding&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;my purple hair dye.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:03.973 --> 00:14:05.278
&lt;i&gt;Nobody knows&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;my real hair color is...&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:05.322 --> 00:14:07.019
&lt;i&gt;An alien bird ate my combadge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:07.063 --> 00:14:08.934
&lt;i&gt;...dropped my tricorder&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;in the toilet again.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:08.978 --> 00:14:10.805
Uh, y-you can just skip
past all that.

00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:13.330
&lt;i&gt;I actually woke myself up,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the gas pains were so bad.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:13.373 --> 00:14:15.027
&lt;i&gt;- I just wish I could fart.&lt;/i&gt;
-

00:14:15.071 --> 00:14:16.768
We can't use these.

00:14:16.811 --> 00:14:18.422
Don't worry, I don't care
that they're embarrassing.

00:14:18.465 --> 00:14:20.293
No, I mean because
they are a joke.

00:14:20.337 --> 00:14:22.426
It's a friggin' blooper reel.
No court's gonna accept this.

00:14:22.469 --> 00:14:23.906
Oh, my God,
I wasted this whole day.

00:14:23.949 --> 00:14:25.733
I can't believe I thought
this was the fix.

00:14:25.777 --> 00:14:28.040
Well, hold on, they do have
the date stamps and locations.

00:14:28.084 --> 00:14:29.824
Starfleet could cross-check
the information.

00:14:29.868 --> 00:14:31.478
Yeah, even if they did,
it would all come down to them

00:14:31.522 --> 00:14:33.132
believing the word
of some goofy ensign.

00:14:33.176 --> 00:14:34.525
When does that ever work out?

00:14:34.568 --> 00:14:36.092
They don't even
believe the captain

00:14:36.135 --> 00:14:37.876
because she's &lt;i&gt;California&lt;/i&gt;-class.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.965
Hey, come on,
they're Starfleet.

00:14:40.009 --> 00:14:41.967
If we can't trust them
to do the right thing,

00:14:42.011 --> 00:14:43.316
what can we trust in?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.579
Yeah, Mariner,
we have to believe.

00:14:47.146 --> 00:14:48.582
Yeah, you guys are right.

00:14:48.626 --> 00:14:50.149
All right,
let's get this PADD to Earth

00:14:50.193 --> 00:14:52.412
and save the day,
Lower Decks-style.

00:14:53.892 --> 00:14:55.763
Hmm.

00:14:55.807 --> 00:14:58.070
I got to, I got to check
the port nacelle real quick.

00:14:58.114 --> 00:14:59.550
You think we're dressed
okay for court?

00:14:59.593 --> 00:15:01.117
I mean, my shirt could be
a little more

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:02.770
- asymmetrical...
-

00:15:02.814 --> 00:15:04.816
Wait, wait, what's going on?
Where is she going?

00:15:04.859 --> 00:15:08.037
She set us on auto-navigation.
I can't stop it.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.516
- She locked us out.
-

00:15:17.046 --> 00:15:19.222
&lt;i&gt;Mariner, what are you doing?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:19.265 --> 00:15:21.006
I'm not going back
until I get hard evidence.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.703
&lt;i&gt;Are you stealing the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos?

00:15:22.747 --> 00:15:24.836
They say she got a bomb
from Klingons? Bull

00:15:24.879 --> 00:15:27.273
I'm gonna go find those Klingons
and bring them back.

00:15:27.317 --> 00:15:28.840
&lt;i&gt;What? -Do you hear yourself right now?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:28.883 --> 00:15:29.884
Look, whatever happens to me,
I'm not gonna

00:15:29.928 --> 00:15:31.234
put you guys through that, okay?

00:15:31.277 --> 00:15:32.235
&lt;i&gt;Wait, wait, wait!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;-Mariner!&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:32.278 --> 00:15:33.671
You don't get it.

00:15:33.714 --> 00:15:34.933
She's your captain,
but she's my mom.

00:15:54.692 --> 00:15:57.129
This is insane. She's gonna
end up in prison, or worse.

00:15:57.173 --> 00:15:59.088
We have to stop her. I don't
care what trouble I get in.

00:15:59.131 --> 00:16:00.089
- Same.
- I want the trouble.

00:16:00.132 --> 00:16:01.438
Give me the trouble.

00:16:01.481 --> 00:16:02.874
If we can't override
the auto-nav,

00:16:02.917 --> 00:16:04.006
we're just gonna
have to lean into it.

00:16:04.049 --> 00:16:06.138
B-But it's taking us back home.

00:16:06.182 --> 00:16:08.923
That's why I redefine what
the shuttle thinks of as "home."

00:16:13.928 --> 00:16:15.713
&lt;i&gt;&lt;i&gt;Yes! You got this, Auto.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:15.756 --> 00:16:18.977
Whoo! We're doing it.
We're...

00:16:19.021 --> 00:16:20.631
We're-we're coming in
a little fast, aren't we?

00:16:20.674 --> 00:16:22.067
Shoot. Auto still thinks
Earth's atmosphere

00:16:22.111 --> 00:16:23.286
is here to slow it down. Uh...

00:16:23.329 --> 00:16:24.635
Hold on.

00:16:29.944 --> 00:16:31.511
-
- Whoa.

00:16:31.555 --> 00:16:34.036
We're alive? Cool.

00:16:35.646 --> 00:16:37.039
W-Wait, what the hell
are you doing?

00:16:37.082 --> 00:16:38.475
I don't want you
getting in trouble.

00:16:38.518 --> 00:16:39.867
And we're not gonna let you

00:16:39.911 --> 00:16:41.086
put yourself in danger. Rutherford.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.566
Oh, no, you don't.

00:16:42.609 --> 00:16:43.610
- You're not thinking straight.
-

00:16:43.654 --> 00:16:44.785
I don't want to hurt you.

00:16:44.829 --> 00:16:46.048
Got her.

00:16:47.701 --> 00:16:50.052
-
Hey, stop it!

00:16:54.882 --> 00:16:58.016
Um, Gary, do we have the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; leaving orbit today?

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.932
What? No. &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is in dry dock. Why?

00:17:11.203 --> 00:17:13.075
-

00:17:13.118 --> 00:17:14.206
Why can't you let me do this?

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:15.947
Why are you so good at fighting?

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.949
Ow, ow, ow.

00:17:22.519 --> 00:17:23.737
&lt;i&gt;&lt;i&gt;There.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:23.781 --> 00:17:25.522
Nav controls are locked.
We're stopped.

00:17:25.565 --> 00:17:26.740
No. No.

00:17:28.046 --> 00:17:29.003
Goddamn it, give me back
the controls.

00:17:29.047 --> 00:17:30.701
I need to... I-I need...

00:17:30.744 --> 00:17:34.531
I need to...

00:17:34.574 --> 00:17:36.794
They put her in handcuffs,

00:17:36.837 --> 00:17:39.884
and I-I couldn't do
a damn thing about it.

00:17:39.927 --> 00:17:41.842
They could take her away
forever, and I can't stop it,

00:17:41.886 --> 00:17:43.279
and I'm just...

00:17:43.322 --> 00:17:45.411
I'm just so scared.

00:17:45.455 --> 00:17:46.804
Hey,

00:17:46.847 --> 00:17:48.284
whatever happens down there,

00:17:48.327 --> 00:17:49.807
we're gonna be right beside you.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.635
Yeah, we're in this together.

00:17:51.678 --> 00:17:52.940
&lt;i&gt;SECURITY OFFICER &lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;USS&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos,

00:17:52.984 --> 00:17:54.681
&lt;i&gt;this is an unauthorized launch.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:54.725 --> 00:17:56.466
&lt;i&gt;What is the nature&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;of your emergency?&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:56.509 --> 00:17:58.511
Oh, crap, it's security.
What do we say? What do we say?

00:17:58.555 --> 00:17:59.817
This is all my fault, okay?

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:01.210
I'll-I'll say
I took you hostage and...

00:18:01.253 --> 00:18:02.385
Wait, look.

00:18:02.428 --> 00:18:04.038
It's the verugament.

00:18:06.171 --> 00:18:09.174
&lt;i&gt;Oh, man, I stopped us right in their path.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:09.218 --> 00:18:11.350
They're incandescent extremophiles.

00:18:11.394 --> 00:18:13.178
They migrate through space
and feed on microscopic...

00:18:13.222 --> 00:18:15.093
They're attacking the ship.

00:18:15.137 --> 00:18:16.747
No, look at this sensor.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:18.314
I-I think they're synthesizing
carbon off the hull,

00:18:18.357 --> 00:18:19.750
and it's triggering
a mass reproductive event.

00:18:19.793 --> 00:18:21.839
&lt;i&gt;&lt;i&gt;It's an orgy?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:21.882 --> 00:18:24.102
Aw, I guess they were in search
of a breeding ground,

00:18:24.146 --> 00:18:26.800
and we're it.
So magical.

00:18:26.844 --> 00:18:28.237
&lt;i&gt;
Cerritos, &lt;i&gt;I repeat,&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.804
&lt;i&gt;this is an unauthorized launch. Please respond.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:30.848 --> 00:18:32.458
Quick, open a channel.

00:18:32.502 --> 00:18:34.460
- What? What're you gonna say?
Just do it!

00:18:34.504 --> 00:18:36.419
This is Ensign D'Vana Tendi

00:18:36.462 --> 00:18:38.551
of the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt; We are
performing a biological survey

00:18:38.595 --> 00:18:40.771
of these reproducing organisms.

00:18:40.814 --> 00:18:42.729
&lt;i&gt;Uh, we're only reading&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;four of you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:42.773 --> 00:18:44.427
That's right.
Everyone else is grounded.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.256
This is a rare scientific event.
We must not be interrupted.

00:18:47.299 --> 00:18:48.735
&lt;i&gt;Interrupted? [stammers]&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;We're coming aboard,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:48.779 --> 00:18:49.823
&lt;i&gt;just stay where you are.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:49.867 --> 00:18:51.303
Okay, uh,

00:18:51.347 --> 00:18:53.653
open the bay doors
and follow me. Come on!

00:18:57.396 --> 00:19:00.269
What the hell
is going on in here?

00:19:00.312 --> 00:19:03.533
Uh, these endangered
creatures need help

00:19:03.576 --> 00:19:05.274
transferring their gametes.

00:19:05.317 --> 00:19:07.537
We're facilitating while we...
...study them.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.366
Uh, doesn't it hurt? Seems like
a lot of charged tentacles.

00:19:10.409 --> 00:19:12.368
Ow. Yeah, no, yeah, it hurts.

00:19:12.411 --> 00:19:15.240
But there's no substitute
for first...

00:19:15.284 --> 00:19:16.546
...firsthand data.

00:19:16.589 --> 00:19:19.375
This is-- Ow!--
just a marvelous-- Ow!--

00:19:19.418 --> 00:19:21.028
specimen. Ouch!

00:19:21.072 --> 00:19:23.117
Okay, I think I've seen
just about enough here.

00:19:23.161 --> 00:19:24.597
Are we under arrest?

00:19:24.641 --> 00:19:27.165
For what? Helping
these precious creatures?

00:19:27.209 --> 00:19:28.253
Of course not.

00:19:28.297 --> 00:19:29.472
And let me just say,

00:19:29.515 --> 00:19:31.343
I love seeing junior officers

00:19:31.387 --> 00:19:32.866
committed to the pursuit
of science.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.477
Yeah, man.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.305
That is us,
just pursuing and doing.

00:19:36.348 --> 00:19:38.176
Super. We'll just need to know
the commander

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.222
who ordered this mission,
and we'll be on our way.

00:19:40.265 --> 00:19:42.049
Uh...

00:19:42.093 --> 00:19:43.529
It's not like
you just stole a starship

00:19:43.573 --> 00:19:45.662
all on your own.
That'd be bananas.

00:19:45.705 --> 00:19:47.403
So, come on, who ordered this?

00:19:47.446 --> 00:19:48.621
Uh...

00:19:48.665 --> 00:19:51.798
I did. Captain Carol Freeman.

00:19:51.842 --> 00:19:53.757
- Mom?
- Thanks, Captain Freeman.

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:56.368
Glad to have you back.

00:19:56.412 --> 00:19:57.891
We're clear.

00:19:57.935 --> 00:19:59.632
What the...

00:19:59.676 --> 00:20:01.243
What are you doing here?
What happened with the trial?

00:20:01.286 --> 00:20:02.244
Are you on the run?

00:20:02.287 --> 00:20:04.028
The trial's over, Beckett.

00:20:04.071 --> 00:20:05.551
It is? How?

00:20:05.595 --> 00:20:07.379
While I was sitting in court,

00:20:07.423 --> 00:20:10.077
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet was carrying out&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;a secret investigation&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:10.121 --> 00:20:11.601
&lt;i&gt;into the Pakled bombing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:11.644 --> 00:20:13.777
&lt;i&gt;Led by Captain Morgan Bateson,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:16.170
&lt;i&gt;this elite team learned&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;of a Pakled connection&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:16.214 --> 00:20:17.955
&lt;i&gt;to a known data fabricator,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:17.998 --> 00:20:19.957
&lt;i&gt;whom they discovered had faked&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.089
&lt;i&gt;the incriminating footage of me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:22.133 --> 00:20:24.614
&lt;i&gt;They pursued&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and captured this forger&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:24.657 --> 00:20:26.616
&lt;i&gt;inside the Romulan Neutral Zone.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:26.659 --> 00:20:29.532
&lt;i&gt;Under some rather&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;invasive questioning&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:29.575 --> 00:20:32.317
&lt;i&gt;from Commander Tuvok,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;this forger revealed&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:32.361 --> 00:20:34.537
&lt;i&gt;the true identity&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;of the bombers,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.669
&lt;i&gt;the Pakleds themselves.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:36.713 --> 00:20:39.063
&lt;i&gt;What?It was a huge reveal.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:39.106 --> 00:20:42.284
&lt;i&gt;Turns out that their plan was to blow up their own capital&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:42.327 --> 00:20:44.764
&lt;i&gt;and frame me&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to force the Federation&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:44.808 --> 00:20:48.768
&lt;i&gt;into relocating them to a more resource-rich planet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:48.812 --> 00:20:53.382
&lt;i&gt;So, it was a classic Pakled&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Samaritan Snare writ large,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:53.425 --> 00:20:55.427
&lt;i&gt;and it would have worked,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:55.471 --> 00:20:57.603
if not for Starfleet's best

00:20:57.647 --> 00:21:00.606
believing in one of their own.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.608
Holy...

00:21:02.652 --> 00:21:04.480
Can we hear that
again, please?

00:21:04.523 --> 00:21:06.177
Wow. Wow.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.787
Starfleet really came through.
Who'd have thought?

00:21:07.831 --> 00:21:09.311
Me, Beckett.

00:21:09.354 --> 00:21:11.922
I told you from the start
to trust in the system.

00:21:11.965 --> 00:21:13.358
I said it this morning.

00:21:13.402 --> 00:21:14.968
I bet your friends
told you just as much.

00:21:15.012 --> 00:21:17.362
Um... they might've said...
I mean, whatever,

00:21:17.406 --> 00:21:19.146
all that matters is
you're free, right, Mom?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.844
All's well that, you know,
turns out fine.

00:21:20.887 --> 00:21:22.889
Oh, no, no,
no, no, missy.

00:21:22.933 --> 00:21:25.065
Do you realize
I was out of court

00:21:25.109 --> 00:21:26.632
for less than an hour

00:21:26.676 --> 00:21:28.373
before I learn that my own

00:21:28.417 --> 00:21:31.376
daughter has stolen my ship
from a military impound?!

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:33.378
You three, go start cleaning

00:21:33.422 --> 00:21:35.119
- whatever the hell this is.
- Uh, well, they're a type of

00:21:35.162 --> 00:21:36.947
incandescent extremoph... Mm...

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.296
Yes, Captain.
Right away, Captain.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:39.602
And you?

00:21:39.645 --> 00:21:41.560
You're with me.

00:21:46.609 --> 00:21:48.567
I blame myself.

00:21:48.611 --> 00:21:50.352
For wearing out that carpet?
Yeah, agreed.

00:21:50.395 --> 00:21:51.396
Beckett, come on.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.876
You see? You see, 'Zo?

00:21:52.919 --> 00:21:55.357
Even now, she thinks
she can just say

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:58.142
and do whatever she wants
with no repercussions.

00:21:58.185 --> 00:21:59.926
'Cause you know what?
She could.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.407
This whole time,
we have covered for her

00:22:02.451 --> 00:22:06.019
and excused her, and now,
we are reaping what we sowed.

00:22:06.063 --> 00:22:08.021
Well, what do you want me
to say? I was trying to help.

00:22:08.065 --> 00:22:10.894
And I love you for that, I do.

00:22:10.937 --> 00:22:13.940
Honey, you have
so much potential,

00:22:13.984 --> 00:22:16.160
but if you're ever
going to amount to anything,

00:22:16.203 --> 00:22:18.945
it won't be because
you saw me as an authority.

00:22:18.989 --> 00:22:20.643
And we know how often
you listen to me.

00:22:20.686 --> 00:22:22.253
Ugh, here we go,
I'm being, what,

00:22:22.296 --> 00:22:23.950
demoted and transferred again?

00:22:23.994 --> 00:22:25.561
Where would you go?

00:22:25.604 --> 00:22:27.824
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is still
your last chance.

00:22:27.867 --> 00:22:30.043
But I can't be the one
to rein you in.

00:22:30.087 --> 00:22:33.264
As your mother, I could never
kick you out of Starfleet.

00:22:33.307 --> 00:22:34.874
However,

00:22:34.918 --> 00:22:38.051
I know someone who
isn't burdened by family ties.

00:22:38.095 --> 00:22:39.879
-
- Come.

00:22:39.923 --> 00:22:40.880
No.

00:22:40.924 --> 00:22:42.099
Not him, not him.

00:22:42.142 --> 00:22:43.840
- No, no, no.
- Ensign Beckett Mariner,

00:22:43.883 --> 00:22:46.320
I'm giving your full
and final oversight

00:22:46.364 --> 00:22:47.887
to Commander Ransom.

00:22:47.931 --> 00:22:50.977
If you do in fact
want to remain in Starfleet,

00:22:51.021 --> 00:22:53.327
it's going to be his call.

00:22:53.371 --> 00:22:54.677
Thank you, Captain.

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:56.505
As far as you're
concerned, Mariner,

00:22:56.548 --> 00:22:58.463
I'm your mama now.

00:23:04.121 --> 00:23:07.211
Ah, you know, even covered
in alien sploof,

00:23:07.254 --> 00:23:08.778
there's no place I'd rather be.

00:23:08.821 --> 00:23:11.520
Yeah. Home, sticky home.

00:23:11.563 --> 00:23:13.217
Oh, hey, turn on FNN.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:15.262
Let's see if they're talking
about the trial.

00:23:15.306 --> 00:23:17.047
&lt;i&gt;We'll talk to the little boy&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:19.832
&lt;i&gt;who solved&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Fermat's last theorem.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:19.876 --> 00:23:22.487
&lt;i&gt;But first, a daring rescue&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;near the moons of Jupiter,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:22.531 --> 00:23:24.794
&lt;i&gt;as a malfunctioning&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;theme park ride&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:24.837 --> 00:23:26.796
&lt;i&gt;leaves one young man&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;traumatized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:26.839 --> 00:23:29.451
No, no, let me go!
I'm Captain Gavin.

00:23:29.494 --> 00:23:31.278
I am on a trek
amongst the stars!

00:24:31.687 --> 00:24:33.689
Chirp.
